cf5ed7debdbbd412f5c0f0253d6d0292a5415" commit_message="QCA6174: Update BT firmware for the chip  This change is to update the stable BT FW to Chromebook platform.  BTFM.RM.1.3-00045-QCARMSWPZ-1 is fully tested onto Windows based PC and is a recommended one by QCA for ChromiumOS with QCA6174 chip.  The firmware was originally published in linux-firmware.git/tree/qca  BUG=b:35578198 TEST=ChromiumOS Partner Eng BT AVL tests on Reef/Electro EVT2 platform.  Change-Id: I88e94b4f7b8d7a9566980bfec5dfce3a8b744165 Signed-off-by: Waldemar Rymarkiewicz &lt;ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/528272 Commit-Ready: Waldemar  Rymarkiewicz &lt;ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com&gt; Tested-by: Waldemar  Rymarkiewicz &lt;ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="528272" owner_email="ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" ref="refs/changes/72/528272/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idb257f0f20422482c729a2b97b4b16ee231ca4d9" commit="ef2ab6af4f13f05e943316dee397e0c1b7edd497" commit_message="stm32f4: Set unique ID properly  Unique device ID register (96 bits) is at a different place on STM32F4 compared to other STM32.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=Using board_read_serial() from hammer/board.c in sweetberry/board.c, confirmed that we can extract and assign a unique USB serial number.  Change-Id: Idb257f0f20422482c729a2b97b4b16ee231ca4d9 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/579575 Commit-Ready: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="579575" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/75/579575/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ib49031ddf96b9b8b447be8348f4fe1041d5d0208" commit="c2e0c9f466f25bb743c7a5ac61a5941ff12217ae" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ath10k: ignore configuring the incorrect board_id  With command to get board_id from otp, in the case of following    boot get otp board id result 0x00000000 board_id 0 chip_id 0   boot using board name 'bus=pci,bmi-chip-id=0,bmi-board-id=0&quot;   ...   failed to fetch board data for bus=pci,bmi-chip-id=0,bmi-board-id=0 from   ath10k/QCA6174/hw3.0/board-2.bin  The invalid board_id=0 will be used as index to search in the board-2.bin.  Ignore the case with board_id=0, as it means the otp is not carrying the board id information.  (cherry picked from commit d2e202c06ca42d353d95df12437740921a6d05b5)  BUG=b:35578198 TEST=Ar10k module loaded and booted properly with 4.4 FW that uses API 6  Change-Id: Ib49031ddf96b9b8b447be8348f4fe1041d5d0208 Signed-off-by: Ryan Hsu &lt;ryanhsu@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Waldemar Rymarkiewicz &lt;ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/568823 Commit-Ready: Waldemar  Rymarkiewicz &lt;ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com&gt; Tested-by: Waldemar  Rymarkiewicz &lt;ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="568823" owner_email="ext.waldemar.rymarkiewicz@tieto.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/23/568823/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib48e2564fcc2553e6a9ff1165c7afdf936196020" commit="53cdb7cccddca24e6d56f53a7912ba6785c6d393" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Continue scanning if sched_scan stops unexpectedly  When scheduled scan stops without the interface request (for example, driver stopped it unexpectedly), start a regular scan to continue scanning for networks and avoid being left with no scan at all.  BUG=b:37954502 TEST=suspend/resume repeatedly and make sure the device seems to be connected from the GUI but is actually not.  Change-Id: Ib48e2564fcc2553e6a9ff1165c7afdf936196020 Signed-off-by: Avraham Stern &lt;avraham.stern@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/506068 Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="506068" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/68/506068/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibd4d30560cc178b27443cea8e56781fb4327dc1d" commit="8801e75f510a7a37a233829e65f565fcedd06062" commit_message="OpenCV: Force to build using libstdc++.  OpenCV does not build when using libc++ in clang. Force it to use libstdc++ for now.  BUG=chromium:747060 TEST=OpenCV builds even libc++ is enabled in clang.  Change-Id: Ibd4d30560cc178b27443cea8e56781fb4327dc1d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/580247 Commit-Ready: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="580247" owner_email="manojgupta@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/47/580247/1" remote="cros" total_